Description: Contribution-adjusted meta-analysis (CAMS) for
    treatment effect modification from modifier-level aggregate data
    (Panaro, Röver & Friede, 2025, arXiv:2512.18785). From paired
    modifier-level estimates per trial, the package builds information
    fractions, fits standard random-effects meta-analysis and
    meta-regression components, and reports interaction, modifier-level,
    and combined-population effects.
    Bayesian inference (default) uses 'bayesmeta'; frequentist inference
    uses 'metafor' (REML/ML). Difference of Averages (DA) and Average
    Difference (AD) are different constructions (Panaro, Röver & Friede,
    2026); the SWADA shared-weight principle is included as context, not
    as an alternative CAMS model.
URL: https://rvpanaro.github.io/interactmeta/, https://arxiv.org/abs/2512.18785
